sami/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertsami/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertsami/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertsami/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2022-10-20T21:46:53Z","updated_at":"2022-11-07T10:53:28Z","closed_at":"2022-11-07T10:53:28Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-3956](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-3956)\r\nCode in `conflict_resolution.cc` and `wait_queue.cc` can live lock with each other in the following scenario:\r\n\r\nt0 -- Call RequestStatusAt for <txn_id> here: https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/blob/57012b642638c3d2669e0d2ea325bdbfc9aee582/src/yb/docdb/wait_queue.cc#L553\r\na request is sent to the coordinator async\r\n\r\nt1 -- Call RequestStatusAt for <txn_id> here:  https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/blob/57012b642638c3d2669e0d2ea325bdbfc9aee582/src/yb/docdb/conflict_resolution.cc#L524\r\nthe callback is stored on the status_waiters_ of the running transaction\r\n\r\nt2 -- RPC returns for <txn_id> and status_waiters_ are invoked in order\r\n\r\nIn this case, the wait_queue.cc callback is triggered first, in which we may attempt to acquire a `LockBatch` before re-running conflict resolution for a waiter. However, if the `LockBatch` for the requested key is already held by conflict resolution, it won't be released until the status_waiter_ corresponding to conflict resolution is resumed, which won't happen until the lock acquisition in wait_queue.cc times out\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"robertsami","id":1457684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTc2ODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1457684?v=4","gravatar_id"